-- FINDING 6 (silent).  A caller that pins the conduct day and forgets the reading day reads the machine's
-- clock, so the answer changes with the day the question is asked, and no diagnostic appears.
-- Run with two --fixed-now values (run-findings.sh does): the same file prints TRUE when the clock says
-- 1 Aug 2012 and FALSE when it says 3 Nov 2026.
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

`TV scheduled` MEANS
    IF `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 2011) AND TODAY AT LEAST (Date 31 10 2012) THEN FALSE ELSE TRUE

-- the reading day is NOT pinned
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (Date 1 6 2011) `TV scheduled`
